  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"43\" data-end=\"194\">The <strong data-start=\"47\" data-end=\"64\">LDL/HDL ratio</strong> is used to assess <strong data-start=\"83\" data-end=\"106\">cardiovascular risk</strong>. It compares the levels of <strong data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"161\">\"bad\" cholesterol (LDL)</strong> to <strong data-start=\"165\" data-end=\"193\">\"good\" cholesterol (HDL)</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>LDL/HDL Ratio</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Risk Level</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt; 2.0</strong></td>\n<td>Ideal / Excellent</td>\n<td>Low cardiovascular risk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>2.0 &ndash; 3.5</strong></td>\n<td>Acceptable / Moderate</td>\n<td>Average risk</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt; 3.5</strong></td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Increased risk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"43\" data-end=\"194\">&nbsp;</p>",
